Mr Marc Lemaître, Director-General for Research and Innovation (RTD). 

73	207	Marc Lemaître studied at Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB) and Bruges (College of 
Europe) and holds a Master in European Economics.
208	354	He  brings 25  years of profound 
experience in European Affairs, both in the European Commission and in the diplomatic 
service of Luxembourg.  

354	517	Between 1996 and 2006, he worked in the Permanent Representation of Luxembourg to the 
European Union, dealing with budgetary, trade and general affairs issues.  

517	670	He joined the Commission in 2007 as Head of the private office of Regional Policy 
Commissioner, Danuta Hübner, and then her successor, Paweł Samecki.  

670	766	Between 2010 and 2013, he led the private office of Budget Commis sioner Janusz 
Lewandowski.  

766	892	Between 2013 and 2016, he managed, as Director, the Office for Administration and Payment 
of individual entitlements (PMO). 

892	990	Between 2016 and January 2023, he  was Director-General for Regional and Urban Policy  
(REGIO). 

990	1069	Since February 2023 he is Director-General for Research and Innovation (RTD). 

